<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Mühlhausen</h1><p class="st-meta">1180 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Mühlhausen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Thuringian imperial city famous as the base of Thomas Müntzer during the Peasants' War and for one of the oldest law books written in German.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhlhausen">Mühlhausen</a> grew around a royal palace and was favoured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperors, gaining the status of an imperial city by about 1180. Around 1200 to 1230 its law was set down in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhlhausen-reichsrechtsbuch">Mühlhausen Reichsrechtsbuch</a>, one of the earliest legal texts in German.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of patricians and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> representatives ruled the city, which grew rich from cloth, woad and trade, joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erfurt">Erfurt</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nordhausen">Nordhausen</a> in a Thuringian city league. In 1525 the radical preacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-muntzer">Thomas Müntzer</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhlhausen">Mühlhausen</a> his base, set up the Eternal League and led its men to defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-frankenhausen">Frankenhausen</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-peasants-war">Peasants' War</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 1525 the city lost its freedom for two decades under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> and Hessian control, regaining imperial status in 1548. It was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1802, belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-westphalia">Kingdom of Westphalia</a> from 1807 to 1813, and then returned to Prussia; it is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1180 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.18%;width:12.38%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1180 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mühlhausen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, then Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mühlhausen in Thüringen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1491&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-muhlhausen" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Mühlhausen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4944 463 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Mühlhausen lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5264 719L5229 694M5264 719L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5264 719h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5264 719h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mühlhausen. <a href="/atlas?year=1491&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-muhlhausen">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
